## Users and the first admin

Payload lets anyone create the first user while the users collection is empty. `{{runScript "ensure-admin"}}` creates the admin from `ADMIN_EMAIL` and `ADMIN_PASSWORD` of `apps/web/.env.admin` when no user exists and does nothing otherwise; `{{runScript "ensure-admin:remote"}}` does the same in the production database, which must happen before the first deploy. `.env.admin` is a file of its own because `build:cf` bundles every `.env*` file of the app into the Worker, and a password has no place there.

## The version of Payload

`payload` and every `@payloadcms/*` package are pinned to one exact version in `apps/web/package.json`, because Payload publishes them together and each adapter checks the version of the core. Move them together. Next.js 16 is built with webpack (`next build --webpack`): Turbopack fails on the server bundle of Payload (payloadcms/payload#16470).
